# Nasij

A smart safety network for large events. A low-cost, reusable bracelet links to the family's phone app, alerts them before a child wanders off, and turns nearby volunteers' phones into a search network with temporary permissions. The bracelet carries no personal data.

## Files

| File | What it is |
|------|------------|
| `App.tsx` | Phone app (React Native / Expo) |
| `app.json` | App settings and permissions |
| `src/theme.ts` | Shared colours, font sizes and styles |
| `src/mock.ts` | Fake data and the agreed data model |
| `nasij_scanner.py` | Laptop scanner (acts as a volunteer device) |

## Step 0: shared files (read before you start)

Everyone builds their screens with fake data first (Phase 1). These two files are shared by all three people.

### `src/theme.ts`: the look

- `C`: colours from the prototype (`C.primary`, `C.danger`, `C.safeBg`, `C.child`, ...)
- `F`: font sizes (`F.title`, `F.h1`, `F.h2`, `F.body`, `F.small`, `F.tiny`)
- `ui`: ready styles: `ui.card`, `ui.row`, `ui.sectionTitle`, `ui.caption`, `ui.text`, `ui.muted`, `ui.btn` / `ui.btnText`, `ui.btnGhost` / `ui.btnGhostText`, `ui.strip` / `ui.stripText`, `ui.dot`

Use these instead of writing colour codes by hand, so the app and the web pages look the same. App text is Arabic: rows use `row-reverse` and text aligns right. The file only has a type import from React Native, so the web pages can import it too.

```ts
import { C, ui } from '../../theme';
<View style={ui.card}><Text style={ui.sectionTitle}>...</Text></View>
```

### `src/mock.ts`: fake data and the data model

**Why:** nobody waits for anybody. The volunteer screens and the dashboard can be built now, before Firebase exists, and every case (lost child, emergency, possible fall, health condition) can be clicked through without a real lost child.

**The types are the contract.** Firebase (Phase 2) copies them exactly, so when the fake data is swapped for live data, the screens do not change. Do not rename or change a field on your own; agree with the team first.

| Type | What it is |
|------|------------|
| `Member` | Person wearing a bracelet: name, `child` or `elder`, age, optional `health`, `braceletId` |
| `Health` | `condition` and `notes` (what a helper should do) |
| `Report` | A case: type `lost`, `emergency` or `fall`; status `open` / `searching` / `closed`; a copy of the member's name, kind and age; photo, `description` (clothing), `health`, `area` and `location`; `assignedVolunteerId`; `closedAs` `found` / `security` |
| `PasserbyReport` | Passer-by tapped the NFC sticker or QR: bracelet number only, no personal data |
| `Volunteer` | Name, on duty, area, location |
| `Sighting` | A volunteer's phone heard a reported bracelet: signal, area and location |
| `Zone` | Area of the event with a centre and radius, for the dashboard map |

The report keeps its own copy of the member's name and health, so a volunteer sees only that one case, and the copy is deleted when the case closes.

Fake lists: `members`, `reports`, `volunteers`, `ME` (the current volunteer), `sightings`, `passerbyReports`, `zones`.

```ts
import { reports } from '../../mock';
const report = reports[0]; // lost child
report.member.name;        // "سنا"
report.description;        // clothing
```

`photo` is a small base64 image stored inside the report (the free Firebase plan has no Storage).

### Folders: edit only your own

| Folder | Owner |
|--------|-------|
| `App.tsx`, `src/screens/family/`, `src/components/`, `src/ble/` | Person 1 |
| `web/report/`, `web/dashboard/`, later `src/firebase/` | Person 2 |
| `src/screens/volunteer/` | Person 3 |

`theme.ts` and `mock.ts` are shared: tell the team before changing them.

## Bracelet

MOKO W6R (shows as `MK Button`), configured with the BeaconX Pro / MK Button app:

- Power saving mode: off
- Double press mode: Alarm info, Alarm mode on, Stay advertising before triggered on

## Run the phone app

```
npx create-expo-app@latest nasij --template blank-typescript
cd nasij
npx expo install react-native-ble-plx expo-dev-client react-native-maps expo-location
```

Replace `App.tsx` and `app.json` with the files in this repo, then:

- First install on iPhone (needs a Mac with Xcode): `npx expo run:ios --device`
- Daily development (Mac or Windows): `npx expo start`

## Run the laptop scanner

```
py -m pip install bleak
py nasij_scanner.py
```
